sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Player as User / Gamer
    participant UI as GamePlay Container (React)
    participant Engine as GameEngine (Pure Functional Core)
    participant WebAudio as Sound Synthesizer
    participant Storage as StorageEngine (v2 Schema)

    Player->>UI: Select game from Catalog (e.g. /play/single/snake)
    UI->>Storage: getPreferences() & getHighScore(gameId)
    Storage-->>UI: Return user settings & best record
    UI->>Engine: getInitialState()
    Engine-->>UI: Return fresh GameState (grid, score=0, active)
    UI-->>Player: Render Canvas / Matrix / Touch D-Pad / HUD

    loop Active Gameplay Frame / Interval
        alt User Input (Keyboard / Touch / Click)
            Player->>UI: KeyDown (Arrow/WASD) or Virtual D-Pad Touch
            UI->>Engine: applyMove(currentState, moveAction)
            Engine-->>UI: Return nextState (new coordinates, score, collisions)
        else Physics / Clock Tick (Snake / Tetris / Breakout)
            UI->>Engine: applyMove(currentState, { type: 'TICK' })
            Engine-->>UI: Return nextState
        end

        opt Event Triggered (Eat, Merge, Clear, Bounce)
            UI->>WebAudio: playSound(effectType, volume)
            WebAudio-->>Player: Real-time Audio Feedback
        end

        UI-->>Player: Re-render updated game canvas / UI HUD
    end

    alt Game Over Condition Reached
        Engine-->>UI: GameState with status='GAME_OVER'
        UI->>WebAudio: playSound('gameover')
        UI->>Storage: recordGamePlay(gameId, finalScore)
        Storage-->>UI: Updated stats & new high score flag
        UI-->>Player: Display Game Over Overlay with Score, Replay & Exit Buttons
        Player->>UI: Click "Play Again" or "Exit to Hub"
    end
